<link rel="stylesheet" href="${com.example.septic.web.AssetPaths.versioned("/research-assets.css")}">
<section class="record-stage-comparison" id="permit-vs-as-built" aria-labelledby="record-stage-heading">
    <h2 id="record-stage-heading">Why do the permit and final drawing show different lengths?</h2>
    <p>A number needs a document stage. In our published Anderson case, the construction permit and later installation record described different lengths.</p>
    <figure class="record-stage-comparison__visual">
        <a href="${com.example.septic.web.AssetPaths.versioned("/images/guides/permit-final-comparison-v1.webp")}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open the reconstructed permit and final-record comparison at full size">
            <img src="${com.example.septic.web.AssetPaths.versioned("/images/guides/permit-final-comparison-v1.webp")}" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Reconstructed case comparison: construction permit planned 300 feet; final record lists 40, 80 and 80 feet, totaling 200 feet. Different document stages retain separate figures.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>Published case findings, visually reconstructed — not original agency documents. <a href="/septic-permit-process/#design-final-case">Read the case →</a></figcaption>
    </figure>
    <dl><div><dt>Construction permit / planned trench</dt><dd><strong>300 ft</strong></dd></div><div><dt>Final record / 40 + 80 + 80 ft</dt><dd><strong>200 ft</strong></dd></div></dl>
    <p><strong>Our answer:</strong> preserve both entries with their dates and stages. Do not average them, assume a typo, or invent why the installation changed. Ask the custodian about unresolved conflicts and later revisions.</p>
    <p><a href="/septic-permit-process/#design-final-case" data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="record_stage_comparison" data-track-target-type="case_study">Read the published comparison and its limits →</a></p>
    <p>These historical figures do not establish the physical layout or current condition.</p>
</section>
